    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T00:46:15Z",
    "body": "Known nit from the re-review, left for the next touch of this code so the green review isn't reset for a comment: `stock_sim.rs` ~98-100 says a NaN or negative radius is \"refused by name\" in `auto_cell`. `auto_cell` (sim `cut.rs:35`) doesn't refuse; its `max` ignores NaN and clamps negatives. Behaviour is unchanged from before this PR, and such radii can't reach it from a real tool, since AddTool validates the diameter. Only the comment overstates it. It will be corrected with M7.3's #586, which rewrites this builder onto `Stock`.",
